1
00:00:02,570 --> 00:00:08,450
{\an2}（A24影业）

2
00:00:12,620 --> 00:00:15,830
{\an2}（纽约中央影业）

3
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:17,870
{\an8}（九码半）

4
00:00:19,790 --> 00:00:20,750
{\an8}（八码半）

5
00:00:29,910 --> 00:00:31,880
- Mrs. Mariann. - You have the nine and a half?
- 玛丽安太太 - 是九码半的吗？

6
00:00:31,890 --> 00:00:33,950
- Yeah, you're a lucky lady. - Oh, I'm excited.
- 是的 可给你找到了 - 太好了

7
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:36,250
Last pair. Let me see those beautiful feet.
最后一双了 来 露个玉足吧

8
00:00:35,430 --> 00:00:37,680
{\an8}（美国 纽约）

9
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:39,910
The right foot's all right?
右脚还可以吧？

10
00:00:39,920 --> 00:00:41,980
There you go. Get it in there.
来 用力伸进去

11
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:44,750
- They're too tight. - It's okay. All right.
- 太小了 - 加油 加油

12
00:00:44,770 --> 00:00:46,830
- Are these the nine and a half? - These are the nine and a half, yeah.
- 这真是九码半？ - 对 九码半

13
00:00:46,840 --> 00:00:48,720
- Do you have the next size? - No, not in a Kerrybrooke.
- 有大一号的吗？ - 唯独这牌子没有

14
00:00:48,730 --> 00:00:50,550
But that's why I don't like Kerrybrooke,
所以我不推荐凯步轩

15
00:00:50,570 --> 00:00:53,030
because they fit really small. They're made for dolls or something.
穿他们鞋 跟裹小脚一样

16
00:00:53,040 --> 00:00:55,920
- They're too tight. - Okay, take 'em off. Don't worry about it.
- 太不合脚了 - 好吧 脱下来吧 脱下来吧

17
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:57,520
- You ever try Vitality? - No.
- 穿过朝阳吗？ - 没有

18
00:00:57,540 --> 00:00:59,800
- It's a much better model if you want durable leather. - I'll be right with you.
- 这牌子档次更高 更耐穿 - 稍等一下

19
00:00:59,820 --> 00:01:01,370
- Excuse me. Sorry. - I'll try it.
- 打扰了 - 拿来试试吧

20
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:04,140
I bought a pair of shoes here the other day from him, with the glasses.
我要找前几天卖我鞋的 戴眼镜的那位

21
00:01:04,150 --> 00:01:05,350
- Marty. - Yeah?
- 马蒂 - 怎么了？

22
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:08,520
This woman said she bought a pair of shoes from you.
有位顾客找你 前几天是你卖她鞋吗？

23
00:01:08,540 --> 00:01:10,590
Oh, yeah. You bought the brown Mary Janes, right?
哦 对 是买了那双棕色玛丽珍吧

24
00:01:10,610 --> 00:01:12,230
- Yeah, I did. They're great. - How do they fit you?
- 没错 鞋挺好的 - 合脚吗？

25
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:13,980
- I wore them out of the store. - Okay.
- 我当时穿着就走了 - 好

26
00:01:13,990 --> 00:01:16,550
- So I left my old ones here. - Okay. What did they look like?
- 然后旧鞋就落在这里了 - 旧鞋长什么样？

27
00:01:16,570 --> 00:01:18,450
They're two-toned pumps, wingtips.
拼色高跟鞋 带小翅膀图案

28
00:01:18,470 --> 00:01:20,370
- Lloyd, did you see her shoes? - No.
- 洛伊 有见到那鞋吗？ - 没有

29
00:01:20,390 --> 00:01:23,200
Is it possible that you maybe put them in one of the boxes of the other shoes
不会被你们装回我没拿走的鞋盒

30
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:25,600
that I was trying on and restocked them?
然后又塞回库房了吧？

31
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:27,740
- Okay. All right. Um... - If I saw the boxes, I'd be able to recognize it.
- 好吧... - 要是看见鞋盒 我就能认出来

32
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:29,740
Do you mind if my colleague helps you out for a second?
让我同事来帮您选购好吗？

33
00:01:29,750 --> 00:01:31,900
Lloyd. Can you help with Mariann here?
洛伊 你帮忙接待一下这位行吗？

34
00:01:31,910 --> 00:01:32,990
Sure. Sure.
没问题 等下

35
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:35,960
- Yeah, we'll check the basement. Come. - Thank you. Excuse me.
- 走 跟我去仓库 - 谢谢 借过

36
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:38,880
- Lloyd's gonna help you. Get the Vitalities. - Okay. I'll think about the price.
- 洛伊会拿来朝阳的 - 好吧 我得考虑下价格

37
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:41,680
- I'll be right with you. Let me finish up here. - Okay, thank you.
- 您先坐会儿 我马上就来 - 好的 谢谢

38
00:01:41,700 --> 00:01:43,260
- What? - Shh.
- 怎么了？ - 嘘

39
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:46,100
- Marty. - Ah, fuck.
- 是马蒂吧？ - 是 真倒霉

40
00:01:46,110 --> 00:01:47,430
I wanna show you something. Come here.
给你看个东西 进来一下

41
00:01:47,450 --> 00:01:49,610
- What? - Just get low. Go low.
- 什么？ - 蹲下 赶紧蹲下

42
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:51,710
Why do I have to get low?
我干嘛非得蹲着啊

43
00:01:53,060 --> 00:01:55,620
- How you doing? - Marty, look what I got for ya.
- 忙吗？ - 马蒂 瞧瞧我给你准备的

44
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:56,880
What is this?
什么东西？

45
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:58,160
Check it out.
仔细瞧瞧

46
00:01:58,220 --> 00:01:59,760
{\an8}（诺金鞋行 家用鞋履 经久耐穿）

47
00:01:59,280 --> 00:02:00,760
What am I looking at?
有啥特别的？

48
00:02:00,770 --> 00:02:02,070
Turn it over.
看看背面

49
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:04,600
{\an8}（马蒂·毛瑟 管事）

50
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:06,000
- Manager? - Manager.
- 做管事？ - 对 管事

51
00:02:06,020 --> 00:02:07,030
Come on, Murray.
得了吧 老默

52
00:02:07,050 --> 00:02:08,930
Whatever you do, just don't tell Lloyd about this.
不管怎样 别告诉洛伊就行

53
00:02:08,950 --> 00:02:11,450
Look, I've been very clear with you. I'm not...
我不是不尊重你 但把话讲明白

54
00:02:11,460 --> 00:02:13,660
trying to be disrespectful. You built something very commendable here.
这店子你经营得确实不错

55
00:02:13,670 --> 00:02:16,200
I don't wanna-- I don't wanna discuss this now.
现在别 别谈这些

56
00:02:16,220 --> 00:02:18,170
Stop. Stop. Let me say something.
别打断我 让我说完

57
00:02:18,190 --> 00:02:20,490
It's been good for my soul to see this up close and personal.
这活确实让我学到不少

58
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:23,070
- But I'm not a shoe salesman. - I don't wanna discuss this.
- 但我不是来卖鞋的 - 我不想听这些

59
00:02:23,090 --> 00:02:25,590
- I'm not a shoe salesman. - I don't wanna discuss this, okay?
- 我不是这块料 - 别扯这些 行吗？

60
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:27,760
I do wanna discuss it, 'cause when I'm back from my trip, this is over.
必须谈 等我飞回来 我就不干了

61
00:02:27,770 --> 00:02:29,000
I'm not coming back and doing this.
我不可能留在这行

62
00:02:29,020 --> 00:02:30,970
Speaking of which, can we settle up now? I gotta buy my plane ticket.
说到这 工钱现在能结吗 我得去买机票

63
00:02:30,990 --> 00:02:32,010
We'll settle at closing.
打烊再结

64
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,520
I wanted to see the travel agent on my lunch break.
我得趁午休去买票

65
00:02:33,540 --> 00:02:35,280
You'll never come back after your lunch break.
你拿到钱肯定不回来了

66
00:02:35,300 --> 00:02:37,240
That's what you think of me?
你真把我看成那种人？

67
00:02:37,250 --> 00:02:39,110
- Yes. - You think I would go and not come back?
- 对 - 你真以为我会跑了不回来吗？

68
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:40,790
Yes. I said settle at closing, okay?
对 我说了打烊再结 行吗？

69
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:42,720
- That's it? - Yeah, that's it. Goodbye.
- 就这样？ - 对 就这样 出去吧

70
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:43,940
I love you.
你可真会疼人

71
00:02:45,490 --> 00:02:47,240
- Come on. - Wait. Just wait for me.
- 快点 - 等我一下

72
00:02:57,880 --> 00:03:01,590
- I was about... I was about to come to you. - What?
- 我本来就...正要去你家的 - 啥？

73
00:03:02,220 --> 00:03:03,810
No, Ira's home sick.
不行 艾勒在家病着呢

74
00:03:03,830 --> 00:03:05,480
- Whoa, whoa, whoa. I can't get sick. - What?
- 喂喂喂 什么病 别传染给我 - 什么？

75
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:06,690
I got the championships.
我得去打锦标赛 我可不能病

76
00:03:06,710 --> 00:03:09,570
No, it's food poisoning. It's food poisoning.
不是 他是吃坏肚子了 只是吃坏肚子了

77
00:03:33,190 --> 00:03:35,690
I wish I could hide you in my luggage.
真想把你塞进行李箱带走

78
00:03:37,470 --> 00:03:39,680
I wanna come with you so bad.
我也好想跟你走

79
00:03:55,190 --> 00:03:58,810
{\an7}♪ Let's dance in style, let's dance for a while ♪
♪ 趁还有机会 跳起来吧 ♪

80
00:03:58,820 --> 00:04:02,270
{\an7}♪ Heaven can wait, we're only watching the skies ♪
♪ 别靠天命 活在当下吧 ♪

81
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:05,330
{\an7}♪ Hoping for the best but expecting the worst ♪
♪ 盼着好事 也做好最坏打算 ♪

82
00:04:05,350 --> 00:04:08,270
{\an7}♪ Are you gonna drop the bomb or not? ♪
♪ 明天会不会就烟消云散？ ♪

83
00:04:09,170 --> 00:04:12,540
{\an7}♪ Let us die young or let us live forever ♪
♪ 要么痛快地死 要么好好活下去 ♪

84
00:04:09,310 --> 00:04:11,650
{\an6}主演
提莫西·查拉梅

85
00:04:12,550 --> 00:04:16,120
{\an7}♪ We don't have the power but we never say never ♪
♪ 命靠天定 但我们偏要逆流而上 ♪

86
00:04:16,130 --> 00:04:19,760
{\an7}♪ Sitting in a sandpit, life is a short trip ♪
♪ 潮来潮去 人生苦短啊 ♪

87
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:19,700
{\an4}主演
格温妮斯·帕特洛

88
00:04:19,770 --> 00:04:22,390
{\an7}♪ The music's for the sad men ♪
♪ 能懂这歌的人 也懂我的伤 ♪

89
00:04:22,450 --> 00:04:25,060
{\an6}主演
敖德萨·阿锡安

90
00:04:23,180 --> 00:04:26,100
{\an7}♪ Can you imagine when this race is won? ♪
♪ 这场竞赛会怎么收场？ ♪

91
00:04:26,730 --> 00:04:30,140
{\an7}♪ Turn our golden faces into the sun ♪
♪ 是胜利还是灭亡？ ♪

92
00:04:27,820 --> 00:04:30,340
{\an4}主演
凯文·奥利里

93
00:04:30,170 --> 00:04:33,140
{\an7}♪ Praising our leaders, we're getting in tune ♪
♪ 我们唱着赞歌 别无选择 ♪

94
00:04:33,150 --> 00:04:36,360
{\an7}♪ The music's played by the, the mad man ♪
♪ 魔鬼弹着舞曲 逼我们起舞 ♪

95
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:35,810
{\an6}主演
泰勒·奥康马

96
00:04:36,610 --> 00:04:38,090
{\an7}♪ Forever young ♪
♪ 永远年轻 ♪

97
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:41,360
{\an4}原创译制
蒙太奇字幕组

98
00:04:38,900 --> 00:04:42,490
{\an7}♪ I want to be forever young ♪
♪ 我想永远年轻 ♪

99
00:04:43,910 --> 00:04:46,910
{\an7}♪ Do you really want to live forever? ♪
♪ 谁不想永远活着？ ♪

100
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:53,180
{\an8}《至尊马蒂 · 美国制造》

101
00:04:46,910 --> 00:04:50,870
{\an7}♪ Forever and ever ♪
♪ 永远永远地活着 ♪

102
00:04:50,870 --> 00:04:53,040
{\an7}♪ Forever young ♪
♪ 永远年轻 ♪

103
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:56,380
{\an7}♪ I want to be forever young ♪
♪ 我想永远年轻 ♪

104
00:04:57,920 --> 00:05:01,380
{\an7}♪ Do you really want to live forever? ♪
♪ 谁不想永远活着？ ♪

105
00:05:01,390 --> 00:05:04,690
Backhand. Backhand. Backhand.
反手 反手 反手

106
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:07,160
Forehand. Forehand. Forehand.
正手 正手 正手

107
00:05:05,280 --> 00:05:07,890
{\an4}演出
法兰·德瑞雪

108
00:05:07,810 --> 00:05:10,640
Backhand. Backhand. Backhand.
反手 反手 反手

109
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:13,900
{\an6}演出
阿贝尔·费拉拉

110
00:05:11,550 --> 00:05:13,930
Forehand. Forehand.
正手 正手

111
00:05:14,990 --> 00:05:16,990
Backhand. Backhand.
反手 反手

112
00:05:16,120 --> 00:05:18,940
{\an4}演出
艾莫里·科恩

113
00:05:17,110 --> 00:05:18,360
And lob.
放高球

114
00:05:19,700 --> 00:05:20,860
Forehand.
正手

115
00:05:21,320 --> 00:05:24,090
{\an6}演出
盖札·罗里格

116
00:05:21,490 --> 00:05:22,880
- Marty! - What!
- 马蒂 - 干嘛

117
00:05:22,890 --> 00:05:24,860
- Phone! - Tell him I left 20 minutes ago!
- 有电话 - 跟他说我20分钟前就走了

118
00:05:24,870 --> 00:05:27,800
I'm not your goddamn messenger! Pick up the goddamn phone!
我才不当你的传声筒 自己去接那该死的电话

119
00:05:27,060 --> 00:05:29,810
{\an4}演出
佩恩·吉列特

120
00:05:27,810 --> 00:05:29,790
I can't. Wally, take the white shirt off.
我跟不上 沃利 把白衬衫脱了

121
00:05:29,810 --> 00:05:31,860
I can't follow the white ball against the white shirt.
白球配白衬衫 看不清

122
00:05:31,870 --> 00:05:34,720
Stop it. You're a fucking sun dodger.
别找借口 孬种才这样找借口

123
00:05:32,420 --> 00:05:34,960
{\an6}演出
桑德拉·伯恩哈德

124
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:36,790
Oh, yeah? I love you. I love you.
我孬种？怎么怕了 怕了？

125
00:05:37,780 --> 00:05:38,860
Hello?
喂

126
00:05:38,870 --> 00:05:40,340
It's Judy.
我是朱迪

127
00:05:39,370 --> 00:05:41,970
{\an4}演出
川口功人

128
00:05:40,730 --> 00:05:42,060
Hi, Judy.
怎么了 朱迪

129
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:43,630
Your mother, she's very sick.
你妈病得很重

130
00:05:43,640 --> 00:05:45,270
- Okay, really? - Yes.
- 真的假的？ - 真的

131
00:05:45,290 --> 00:05:47,420
She's gray in the face. She's speaking nonsense.
她脸色苍白 满嘴胡话

132
00:05:46,790 --> 00:05:49,460
{\an4}演出
拉瑞·拉索·斯洛曼

133
00:05:47,430 --> 00:05:49,290
She's asking for you. You should come home.
她一直喊你 你得赶快回家一趟

134
00:05:49,310 --> 00:05:52,530
Sounds really bad. You should probably call an ambulance.
听上去不行了 你们赶紧叫救护车吧

135
00:05:53,300 --> 00:05:55,940
{\an4}演出
卢克·曼利

136
00:05:53,350 --> 00:05:54,670
Who's gonna go with her?
谁陪她去啊

137
00:05:54,680 --> 00:05:57,200
Uh, I don't know. You should probably go since you're so invested.
我不知道 你这么上心 你陪她去呗

138
00:05:57,940 --> 00:05:59,390
Hold on a minute.
等一下 别挂

139
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,480
He's not buying it.
他不吃这套

140
00:06:00,490 --> 00:06:02,200
Just tell him I stopped breathing!
跟他说我断气了

141
00:06:01,250 --> 00:06:04,960
{\an8}（至尊马蒂 美国制造）

142
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:04,980
Absolutely not. That's ridiculous. I'm not saying that.
绝对不行 太严重了 我不能这么说

143
00:06:04,990 --> 00:06:07,180
Tell him you're taking me to the hospital.
跟他说你正急着送我去医院

144
00:06:07,200 --> 00:06:09,450
Okay, fine. I'll take her to the emergency room
好吧 我得赶紧把她送去急诊

145
00:06:09,470 --> 00:06:11,570
and sit there and wait for God knows how long.
然后在那儿陪着 天知道要陪多久

146
00:06:11,580 --> 00:06:14,250
And you can come here and give my husband his medicine
你来负责伺候我丈夫 给他喂药

147
00:06:14,260 --> 00:06:16,740
and massage his feet all night long.
“晚上给他翻身做按摩”

148
00:06:16,750 --> 00:06:18,290
Tell him I passed out.
“跟他说我晕倒了”

149
00:06:17,150 --> 00:06:19,590
{\an4}配乐
丹尼尔·洛帕汀

150
00:06:18,300 --> 00:06:21,010
- Oh, my God! Your mother, she just lost consciousness. - Hi, sweetheart.
- “天呐 你妈刚刚昏过去了” - 你好啊 小姑娘

151
00:06:21,030 --> 00:06:22,990
You've gotta come home now.
“你现在赶紧回家”

152
00:06:24,500 --> 00:06:25,600
Hello?
谁啊

153
00:06:25,620 --> 00:06:28,000
Hi. Just give me a second.
是我 饭马上好

154
00:06:30,010 --> 00:06:31,800
I don't know what you want me to say, Judy.
“朱迪 别闹了行吗”

155
00:06:31,810 --> 00:06:33,270
I'm busy. I'm on my lunch break.
“我正忙着 连午饭都还没吃呢”

156
00:06:33,290 --> 00:06:36,230
I can hear her whispering. She's right there standing next to you.
“我妈就在你旁边指挥 我都听得见”

157
00:06:36,250 --> 00:06:38,850
- I told you she passed out. - It's annoying me now.
- “我都说她昏过去了” - “别来烦我了”

158
00:06:38,870 --> 00:06:40,270
Who are you talking to?
跟谁通话呢？

159
00:06:40,280 --> 00:06:42,770
Oh. I'm not talking to anybody.
哦 没人

160
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:45,420
Judy's just been tying up the line for an hour.
朱迪一直占着电话好久了

161
00:06:45,440 --> 00:06:47,330
I got you some broth.
我给你买了点热饭

162
00:06:46,660 --> 00:06:49,200
{\an4}剪辑
罗纳德·布隆斯坦
乔什·萨弗迪

163
00:06:50,390 --> 00:06:51,510
It's ice cold.
都凉透了

164
00:06:51,530 --> 00:06:54,210
- Yeah, 'cause the line was really long at the shop. - Oh, yeah?
- 买饭排了好久 买回来都凉了 - 你都不打草稿？

165
00:06:54,230 --> 00:06:56,070
So that's what they'll say if I call down and ask?
信不信我现在打电话去核实？

166
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:57,830
You don't believe me? You calling me a liar?
你要是觉得我骗你

167
00:06:57,850 --> 00:06:59,130
Pick up the phone and call them.
你就打电话核实去

168
00:06:59,150 --> 00:07:02,200
- You're gonna have to get Judy off the phone first. - Oh, okay.
- 不过看你怎么打 朱迪在占着电话 - 喔 行

169
00:07:02,220 --> 00:07:04,100
Hey, Judy, get off the phone.
喂 朱迪 把电话给我挂掉

170
00:07:09,760 --> 00:07:12,120
{\an6}摄影
达吕斯·康第

171
00:07:15,350 --> 00:07:18,100
Okay, this is a normal IATT approved ball.
看 这颗是国际乒联标准球

172
00:07:15,350 --> 00:07:20,150
{\an8}【国际乒乓球联合会:1926年成立 主管国际乒乓球赛事和规则】

173
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:20,170
Try to follow the white ball against the white.
盯紧这颗白球

174
00:07:21,730 --> 00:07:23,090
Almost impossible, right?
在白背景下挺难的吧

175
00:07:23,110 --> 00:07:24,710
I don't even see your eyes moving.
你眼珠都没动

176
00:07:24,730 --> 00:07:26,850
If I'm wearing a white shirt, you can't see the ball.
要是我穿白衬衫 你连球都看不到

177
00:07:26,870 --> 00:07:29,590
Now, imagine it with an orange ball, which no one's ever thought of.
换颗橙球试试 这是我自个儿想出来的

178
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:31,580
See? You're already following it way better. Look at his eyes.
看吧 你盯得多牢 瞧他那眼神

179
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:33,280
- See how his eyes are looking? - Yeah, I see it.
- 看见没？ - 嗯 看见了

180
00:07:33,300 --> 00:07:34,660
You're looking more engaged now.
你现在盯得更紧了

181
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:36,540
So that's what we wanna do. Right now in the world of table tennis,
这就是机遇所在 目前桌球界

182
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:39,080
{\an8}【桌球:英语中乒乓球亦称“桌上网球” 简称桌球】

183
00:07:36,560 --> 00:07:39,080
you're obliged to wear black, just so you can follow the white ball.
为了盯住白球都得穿黑衣

184
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:41,680
- Look at this. That's Ted Bailey. - Who's that?
- 看看这个 这是泰德·贝利 - 他是谁？

185
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:43,760
{\an8}【桌上网球为正式运动称谓 乒乓球偏休闲用语】

186
00:07:41,700 --> 00:07:43,780
That's ex-number one ranked player in the world right now.
他曾是英国冠军 世界第一

187
00:07:43,800 --> 00:07:45,960
He's the British champion. I've already beat him, by the way.
已经被我打败了

188
00:07:45,970 --> 00:07:47,080
Now look at this.
再看这个

189
00:07:47,090 --> 00:07:49,210
That's Jack Kramer, number one tennis player.
网球界第一杰克·克雷默

190
00:07:47,090 --> 00:07:51,420
{\an8}【杰克·克雷默:40-50年代著名网球手 推动网球精英化】

191
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:51,400
- What's the difference there? - He's wearing all white.
- 有啥区别？ - 他穿的是全白

192
00:07:51,420 --> 00:07:53,050
He's in all white. It's beautiful.
对 一身白 很绅士

193
00:07:51,420 --> 00:07:55,560
{\an8}【50年代网球为绅士运动 桌上网球(乒乓球)尚非主流】

194
00:07:53,060 --> 00:07:55,550
To me, that's luxury. To me, that's class. You could sell that.
这叫品味 这叫格调 这是卖点

195
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:59,050
Marty, a custom ball like that is gonna cost a lot of money.
马蒂 这种定制球得花不少钱

196
00:07:59,060 --> 00:08:01,390
Of course it's custom. It's an original ball for an original guy.
当然得定制 奇人配奇球

197
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,320
It's the Marty Supreme ball, not the Marty Normal ball.
这是至尊马蒂牌 不是平庸马蒂牌

198
00:08:03,340 --> 00:08:04,480
But what's it gonna cost?
你算过成本吗？

199
00:08:04,510 --> 00:08:06,450
It doesn't matter the cost. We can't cheap out on this.
钱不重要 咱别抠门

200
00:08:06,460 --> 00:08:08,070
It's gonna be nominal, Mr. Galanis.
花不了多少钱的 加拉尼斯先生

201
00:08:08,090 --> 00:08:10,430
You always said we gotta spend money to make money, right?
你不是老说先花钱才能赚钱吗

202
00:08:09,420 --> 00:08:11,900
{\an4}制片人
提莫西·查拉梅

203
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:11,700
Get me a cup of coffee.
给我端杯咖啡来

204
00:08:11,720 --> 00:08:13,750
No. Get your secretary to get ya a cup of coffee.
没门 让你秘书去弄

205
00:08:13,770 --> 00:08:15,610
Nancy's busy. Just get me a coffee.
南希忙着呢 你去弄吧

206
00:08:15,620 --> 00:08:17,500
Dad, we're talking like men about business here.
才不 我正像大人那样谈生意

207
00:08:17,520 --> 00:08:20,910
- I'm not getting ya a cup of coffee. - Get me the damn coffee!
- 我才不给你端咖啡 - 赶紧去给老子端咖啡去

208
00:08:24,010 --> 00:08:26,540
{\an6}制片人
安东尼·卡塔格斯

209
00:08:26,600 --> 00:08:27,680
Marty, you want a coffee?
马蒂 也给你来一杯？

210
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:29,890
No, I'm all right. I'm not drinking caffeine.
谢谢 不用了 我不碰咖啡因

211
00:08:33,000 --> 00:08:34,000
Listen.
听着

212
00:08:34,790 --> 00:08:38,450
I appreciate you're friends with my son.
我感谢你和我儿子的这份交情

213
00:08:38,470 --> 00:08:40,680
He's limited.
但他不成器

214
00:08:40,690 --> 00:08:42,520
He's 30 years old. He's still living at home.
30岁还靠爹吃饭

215
00:08:42,540 --> 00:08:44,190
He hasn't done much.
没啥名堂

216
00:08:44,210 --> 00:08:47,270
And he doesn't know business. He doesn't know the costs.
他也不懂做生意 就会乱花钱

217
00:08:47,290 --> 00:08:49,650
I don't think he's limited, Mr. Galanis, respectfully.
恕我直言 盖拉尼斯先生 我不觉得他不成器

218
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:51,570
I mean, look at your business success.
看看您做生意的本事

219
00:08:51,590 --> 00:08:53,620
That's in your DNA, and you passed that through to Dion.
那是刻在骨子里的 迪翁也有

220
00:08:53,640 --> 00:08:55,730
- It just hasn't been awoken yet. - I don't know.
- 只是还没显露出来 - 谁知道呢

221
00:08:55,740 --> 00:08:58,080
I wouldn't be here trying to involve you in something that I
我要是没把握

222
00:08:56,370 --> 00:08:58,870
{\an4}制片人
伊莱·布什
罗纳德·布隆斯坦
乔什·萨弗迪

223
00:08:58,100 --> 00:09:00,350
didn't fully in my bones believe in.
我也不会拉您入伙的

224
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:03,160
And I have tremendous respect for your money. I know it's hard to believe,
我很尊重您的钱 说来您可能不信

225
00:09:03,170 --> 00:09:05,960
but I'm telling you, this game, it fills stadiums overseas.
但这门运动在国外是火得不得了

226
00:09:05,980 --> 00:09:09,000
And it's only a matter of time before it fills stadiums in the United States too,
在美国火起来也只是时间问题

227
00:09:09,010 --> 00:09:12,040
before I'm staring at you from the cover of a Wheaties box.
到时候我的广告会铺天盖地

228
00:09:12,290 --> 00:09:14,290
I- I don't know nothing about this business.
我 我对这行一窍不通

229
00:09:14,300 --> 00:09:16,260
No, you don't. That's why you gotta trust me.
确实不通 所以更该信我

230
00:09:16,270 --> 00:09:19,340
This time next week, I'll be the first American to ever win the British Open.
下周这个时候 我就是首位赢下英国公开赛的美国人

231
00:09:16,500 --> 00:09:18,960
{\an4}编剧
罗纳德·布隆斯坦
乔什·萨弗迪

232
00:09:19,350 --> 00:09:22,130
That'll slide me into the number one ranking for the World Championship.
到时候我就能一路杀到世锦赛 然后拿下世界第一

233
00:09:22,140 --> 00:09:24,470
Life magazine's gonna cover it. Look magazine's gonna cover it.
到时候《生活》和《展望》都会报道

234
00:09:24,490 --> 00:09:28,680
They have to. The editor of Look magazine, he loves me. They all love me.
这是板上钉钉的事 《展望》就在捧我 他们都会捧我

235
00:09:28,690 --> 00:09:33,900
I'm uniquely positioned to be the face of the entire sport in the United States.
到时候我就是这项运动在美国的唯一代言人

236
00:09:31,150 --> 00:09:33,370
{\an4}导演
乔什·萨弗迪

237
00:09:31,880 --> 00:09:34,880
{\an8}（家庭鞋履）

238
00:09:41,150 --> 00:09:42,460
Lloyd!
洛伊

239
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,300
I'm closing up.
我要打样

240
00:09:52,320 --> 00:09:54,330
Yeah, I can see that. Just here to see my uncle.
我知道 我来找我舅

241
00:09:54,340 --> 00:09:55,420
He left.
他走了

242
00:09:55,440 --> 00:09:58,210
He left? What do you mean he left? For the day?
走了？你什么意思？不回来了？

243
00:09:59,880 --> 00:10:01,470
He had to take your mother to the hospital.
他得带你妈去医院

244
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:03,590
For crying out loud. She's not sick.
别闹了 她根本没病

245
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:05,890
Hey, Lloyd, he owes me money. We were supposed to settle up today.
洛伊 他还欠我工钱 说好了今天结清

246
00:10:05,900 --> 00:10:08,230
Well, maybe if you didn't take that five-hour lunch,
要不是你午休了五个钟头

247
00:10:08,250 --> 00:10:10,160
- you would have spoke with him. - Oh, shut up.
- 兴许就能见着他 - 闭嘴吧你

248
00:10:28,580 --> 00:10:31,230
- Hello. - You're sounding a lot better, huh? That happened quick.
- 谁呀 - 吃了什么狗皮膏药 好得挺快的啊

249
00:10:31,240 --> 00:10:33,140
I'll live, no thanks to you!
我会挺过去的 别指望我靠你

250
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:36,120
Enough, Mom. Are you with Murray? Be honest.
妈 别扯了 默里舅在你那儿吗？别骗我

251
00:10:36,720 --> 00:10:39,630
No. I think he left for his trip. Okay?
没有 但他好像准备出趟远门

252
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:41,260
His trip? What trip?
出哪门子的远门？

253
00:10:41,270 --> 00:10:44,120
He's taking Esther to Kutchers for the weekend.
他带着埃丝特要去库彻度假村过周末

254
00:10:44,130 --> 00:10:46,800
- When this... - But he would have stayed if I asked him to.
- 这算什么啊 - 只要我一句话 他就会留下

255
00:10:46,810 --> 00:10:50,500
You're not sick, Mom. He was supposed to give me my money for my flight.
你根本没病 妈 他答应给我机票钱的

256
00:10:50,510 --> 00:10:52,890
Well, I don't know anything about that, sweetie.
孩子 那事我可不知道

257
00:10:52,900 --> 00:10:54,900
Yes, you do! Why do you think I'm working here?
别装蒜 否则我干嘛干这活？

258
00:10:54,910 --> 00:10:57,190
I literally only accepted this job for that.
我就是为了挣那笔钱

259
00:10:57,200 --> 00:11:00,110
I have no idea what you are implying.
我可比窦娥还冤

260
00:11:00,120 --> 00:11:01,820
- You know what this is? - What, what is this?
- 你知道你在干嘛吗？ - 我在干嘛？

261
00:11:01,830 --> 00:11:04,110
This is sabotage. You're sabotaging me.
你在毁我 你在毁我前程

262
00:11:04,120 --> 00:11:06,870
Oh, please. You're sabotaging your own life.
别扯了 你是在自毁前程

263
00:11:14,330 --> 00:11:16,310
- What is that? - What?
- 那是什么？ - 什么？

264
00:11:16,510 --> 00:11:18,590
Are you seriously thinking I'm gonna rob you?
你竟然觉得我要抢你？

265
00:11:18,600 --> 00:11:19,670
Just a reflex.
职业反应

266
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:22,220
If I wanted to rob you, you'd be dead. You'd be in a pool of blood.
我要真想抢你 你早死在血泊里了

267
00:11:22,240 --> 00:11:25,120
I came to grab my suit. You know I bought this specifically for my trip?
我是来拿西装的 这是我特地为这趟比赛买的

268
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:27,950
Didn't know you need a suit to play ping pong.
打小乒乓还要穿西装 真长见识了

269
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:29,110
{\an8}【乒乓:1950年代“乒乓”在部分场合带有嘲讽意味】

270
00:11:29,120 --> 00:11:31,800
{\an8}【从事这项运动常被歧视 被视为不务正业】

271
00:11:36,910 --> 00:11:39,450
I just want the $700 that Murray owes me.
我就要老默欠我的那700块

272
00:11:36,910 --> 00:11:40,530
{\an8}【约合2026年 8,600美元 6万人民币 26万新台币】

273
00:11:39,470 --> 00:11:40,530
Yeah, or what?
不然呢？

274
00:11:40,550 --> 00:11:42,450
- Or I'm gonna shoot you in the leg. - No you're not.
- 不然我就往你腿上来一枪 - 你不敢

275
00:11:42,470 --> 00:11:43,530
You sure about that?
你敢赌吗？

276
00:11:43,540 --> 00:11:45,870
You shoot me in the leg, you'll be spending the next few years in jail.
你要是打我腿 你未来几年都得坐牢

277
00:11:45,890 --> 00:11:47,320
Okay, I'll shoot you in the head instead.
行 那我就朝你脑门开枪

278
00:11:47,330 --> 00:11:48,530
You're not gonna do that either.
你没那胆子

279
00:11:48,540 --> 00:11:51,240
Look, Lloyd, I just want what was promised to me, not a penny more.
洛伊 听我说 我只拿走我的那700 绝不多拿

280
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:53,540
I'm gonna be coming home with ten times that amount in prize money.
回来我会带回十倍奖金

281
00:11:53,550 --> 00:11:55,620
So just turn the other cheek, let me take what I'm owed,
睁只眼闭只眼吧 让我拿走欠我的

282
00:11:55,630 --> 00:11:57,420
and I'll give you an even $100 dollars when I get back.
等我回来给你整整100

283
00:11:55,630 --> 00:11:59,050
{\an8}【约1,230美元 8,600人民币 3.7万新台币】

284
00:11:57,430 --> 00:11:59,040
Not interested.
不干

285
00:11:59,050 --> 00:12:01,180
Lloyd, come on. Look at me, please.
洛伊 别这样 转过来

286
00:12:01,190 --> 00:12:04,470
We both know you'd love nothing more than to see my ass get canned.
咱俩都清楚 你巴不得看我卷铺盖走人

287
00:12:04,480 --> 00:12:07,090
You're a thousand times more motivated than me to do this job,
你干这行的劲头比我大千万倍

288
00:12:07,110 --> 00:12:08,690
and yet look at this, okay?
可你看看吧

289
00:12:08,710 --> 00:12:10,110
Look.
看看

290
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:13,120
Murray gave that to me. Flip it over.
老默给我的 看看背面

291
00:12:13,140 --> 00:12:16,070
Manager. I'm gonna be your boss!
管事 我要当你管事了

292
00:12:16,090 --> 00:12:19,360
How unfair is that? I could fire you whenever I want.
公平吗？我能把你扫地出门

293
00:12:19,380 --> 00:12:21,720
I could tell you to sweep the floor on your hands and knees.
还能叫你跪着扫地

294
00:12:21,730 --> 00:12:23,260
How about that, okay?
任我差遣

295
00:12:24,130 --> 00:12:27,270
Lloyd, I'm actually pointing a gun at you right now.
洛伊 我真拿枪指着你

296
00:12:27,290 --> 00:12:29,200
I'm actually threatening to use it.
真的在威胁你

297
00:12:29,210 --> 00:12:32,080
This is a legit robbery like any other. My fingerprints are all over this thing.
这是实打实的抢劫 枪上有我的指纹

298
00:12:32,090 --> 00:12:33,370
These are facts.
这都是铁证

299
00:12:33,380 --> 00:12:35,670
So open the safe, let me take what I'm owed,
把钱柜打开 把该我的给我

300
00:12:35,690 --> 00:12:37,820
and you can call Murray, tell him exactly what happened,
回头你照实跟老默说

301
00:12:37,830 --> 00:12:40,900
get me fired, press charges. Whatever you want, okay?
想把我轰走还是告我都随你 行吗？

302
00:12:43,340 --> 00:12:44,720
Fine.
行

303
00:12:52,350 --> 00:12:54,470
- Here you go, sir. - Thank you.
- 给您 先生 - 谢谢

304
00:12:54,480 --> 00:12:56,820
{\an7}♪ The time I like is the rush hour ♪
♪ 我爱高光时刻 ♪

305
00:12:57,400 --> 00:12:58,930
{\an7}♪ 'Cause I like the rush ♪
♪ 我爱人群喧嚣 ♪

306
00:12:59,820 --> 00:13:01,910
{\an7}♪ The pushing of the people ♪
♪ 人群拥挤又吵闹 ♪

307
00:13:00,770 --> 00:13:01,990
You son of...
垃圾

308
00:13:02,820 --> 00:13:04,370
{\an7}♪ I like it all so much ♪
♪ 我就沉浸其中 ♪

309
00:13:05,240 --> 00:13:07,290
{\an7}♪ Such a mass of motion ♪
♪ 人潮蜂拥涌过来 ♪

310
00:13:07,830 --> 00:13:09,830
{\an7}♪ Do not know where it goes ♪
♪ 谁晓得要去哪儿 ♪

311
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:13,210
{\an7}♪ I move with the movement ♪
♪ 我随人群往前走 ♪

312
00:13:11,630 --> 00:13:13,080
We don't get our own rooms?
还没有单间吗？

313
00:13:13,140 --> 00:13:15,790
{\an8}（英国 伦敦）

314
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:16,800
{\an7}♪ And I have the touch ♪
♪ 尽情享受这感觉 ♪

315
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:16,750
It's freezing in here.
这里还冷得要死

316
00:13:17,420 --> 00:13:21,760
I really need you to be serious now. Eyes on me.
现在给我正经点儿 眼睛看这里

317
00:13:21,780 --> 00:13:23,340
Pakistan, I need you to look at me.
巴基斯坦 看这里

318
00:13:23,350 --> 00:13:25,560
Wait, Japan brought a team this year? You see that?
日本今年也派队来了？瞧见没？

319
00:13:25,580 --> 00:13:28,230
Yeah. The Japs sent a team.
是啊 小日本也来了

320
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:29,730
What about the travel ban?
出境管制呢？

321
00:13:28,240 --> 00:13:32,040
{\an8}【1952年随盟军移交日本主权 出入境管制开始放宽】

322
00:13:29,750 --> 00:13:32,020
- They must have lifted it. - No more travel ban?
- 肯定解禁了 - 出境管制解除了？

323
00:13:32,040 --> 00:13:35,610
Okay, gentlemen, I want you to flip your paddles for me now.
各位 现在把球拍翻过来 露出国旗

324
00:13:35,630 --> 00:13:36,850
Thank you very much.
谢谢配合

325
00:13:37,220 --> 00:13:40,440
Here we go. One. Two. Three.
准备 一 二 三

326
00:13:38,740 --> 00:13:40,700
{\an7}♪ Shake those hands ♪
♪ 握个手吧 ♪

327
00:13:40,990 --> 00:13:42,200
Hold it still.
别动

328
00:13:41,510 --> 00:13:43,000
{\an7}♪ Shake those hands ♪
♪ 握个手吧 ♪

329
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:45,790
{\an7}♪ Shake hands ♪
♪ 握手 ♪

330
00:13:44,670 --> 00:13:45,980
{\an8}（第一场）

331
00:13:47,020 --> 00:13:48,380
{\an7}♪ Shake hands ♪
♪ 握手 ♪

332
00:13:55,790 --> 00:13:57,550
Match point, Mauser.
马蒂·毛瑟 赛点

333
00:13:57,570 --> 00:14:02,630
{\an8}【赛点:率先达到者只需再得一分即可赢下整场比赛】

334
00:14:02,650 --> 00:14:10,230
{\an8}【1950年代乒乓球普遍采用每局21分制 比赛多为五局三胜】

335
00:14:19,270 --> 00:14:21,630
Match, Mauser.
马蒂·毛瑟 胜出

336
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:28,400
You let me get to my forehand too much. Should've tried to put me in my backhand.
你给我太多正手机会了 应该逼我打反手

337
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:28,430
{\an8}【正手/反手:在乒乓球中正手利于进攻 反手偏防守】

338
00:14:28,430 --> 00:14:30,070
Point, Endo.
远藤 得分

339
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:52,160
Point, Endo.
远藤 得分

340
00:14:57,930 --> 00:15:00,470
- What's the score here? - Nineteen-four.
- 几比几了？ - 19比4

341
00:15:00,480 --> 00:15:03,390
- The Japanese guy? - Japanese guy's trashing Bailey.
- 日本人领先？ - 那日本小子在揍烂贝利

342
00:15:03,950 --> 00:15:05,910
What's he using? What's that paddle?
他手里是什么？那是什么球拍？

343
00:15:05,930 --> 00:15:08,180
I don't know, mate. No one knows.
不知道 没人见过

344
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:11,990
It's silent.
没声音

345
00:15:12,010 --> 00:15:14,340
- Like a ghost! - Wow.
- 静得出奇 - 哇

346
00:15:14,880 --> 00:15:16,240
Fuck, Bailey.
贝利 好好打

347
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:18,220
Point, Endo.
远藤 得分

348
00:15:19,170 --> 00:15:20,880
Match point.
赛点

349
00:15:30,360 --> 00:15:32,580
{\an8}（第三场）

350
00:15:32,600 --> 00:15:33,700
Two games.
还剩两局

351
00:15:40,240 --> 00:15:41,660
21-9.
21比9

352
00:15:57,290 --> 00:15:58,380
- Great game. - Great game, Marty.
- 打得好 - 打得好 马蒂

353
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:00,070
Match, Mauser.
马蒂·毛瑟 胜出

354
00:16:16,760 --> 00:16:19,500
The winners of the tournament at Stockholm...
那些在斯德哥尔胜出的人...

355
00:16:19,520 --> 00:16:22,850
Hey. You're Ram Sethi, right?
嘿 你是拉姆·塞西吧

356
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:24,270
Sorry, could you hold for a moment?
抱歉 您先等会儿

357
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:26,560
- You don't mind? - No. Can I help you with something?
- 你不介意吧？ - 请说 你有啥事？

358
00:16:26,570 --> 00:16:28,810
I was just curious, where are you staying while you're in town?
打听个事 你们住在哪家酒店？

359
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:30,770
- What business is it of yours? - No.
- 这关你什么事？ - 没事

360
00:16:30,780 --> 00:16:32,440
I'm just saying, what hotel are you staying at?
就是随便打听下

361
00:16:32,460 --> 00:16:34,860
All the IATT representatives are stationed at the Ritz.
国际乒联的官员都住丽兹酒店

362
00:16:34,870 --> 00:16:37,240
- At the Ritz? Yeah, that's what I heard. - Yes.
- 丽兹酒店？别人也这么说 - 对

363
00:16:37,250 --> 00:16:39,410
- Do you think that's okay? - I don't know what you're implying.
- 就这么定了 你没意见吧？ - 什么就这么定了？

364
00:16:39,430 --> 00:16:41,810
- Have you seen where they put me? - Is it a problem?
- 你见过我住的那地方吗？ - 有啥问题吗？

365
00:16:41,820 --> 00:16:44,990
Well, with all due respect, sir, it's a dump.
客气说 那地方就是个狗窝

366
00:16:45,010 --> 00:16:47,660
I'm so sorry it doesn't meet your high standards.
很抱歉没有让你满意

367
00:16:47,670 --> 00:16:50,490
We offer complimentary housing to all our players, Mr. Mauser.
我们这儿给所有选手都是统一标准

368
00:16:50,510 --> 00:16:52,820
So far as I know, you're the only one to complain.
你是唯一一个来这抱怨的

369
00:16:52,840 --> 00:16:54,890
You're talking to me like I'm any player off the street, okay?
你这口气 别把我当普通选手 好吗？

370
00:16:54,910 --> 00:16:57,130
I need good rest so I can win the tournament.
我得休息好 才能赢下比赛

371
00:16:57,140 --> 00:16:59,840
You know perfectly well what an American win will do for the future of the sport.
你很清楚美国人赢对这项运动的好处

372
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:03,030
- I'm good for table tennis, Mr. Sethi. - Appeal to the USTTA.
- 我就是未来桌球的代言人 - 那就向美乒协反映呗

373
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:05,720
There is no USTTA. The USTTA is two guys and a desk. It doesn't exist.
美乒协有用吗？他们整个机构就那俩人

374
00:17:05,730 --> 00:17:07,310
- Well, that's not my problem. - It is your problem.
- 那就不归我管了 - 就归你管

375
00:17:07,330 --> 00:17:09,600
I wanna stay where you're staying! That's what I need!
我要住你住的那家酒店 就这么简单

376
00:17:09,610 --> 00:17:12,440
I am finding this whole exchange really offensive.
您这番言论实在是太失礼了

377
00:17:12,450 --> 00:17:13,900
- You're offended? - I am offended.
- 我失礼？ - 对 您失礼

378
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:17,760
I'm offended! You're making your star player huddle in a rat's ass!
你们才失礼呢 让明星选手住狗窝

379
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:19,660
I'm so sorry for that interruption.
抱歉刚才被打断了

380
00:17:19,680 --> 00:17:22,530
Um, back to Ceylon and Mexico...
那咱们接着说锡兰和墨西哥的事...

381
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:26,320
- This is a nice hotel. Must cost a mint. - Yeah, very nice.
- 这酒店真不赖 肯定很贵 - 是啊 确实不错

382
00:17:26,330 --> 00:17:28,590
The IATT covers accommodations?
是国际乒联报销的吗？

383
00:17:28,610 --> 00:17:31,940
- Only for their star players. - Is that right? How many are there?
- 明星选手才有这种待遇 - 是吗？那有多少名啊

384
00:17:31,950 --> 00:17:35,240
Star players? I don't know. I haven't seen any others, so one.
明星选手？不知道 听说就一个

385
00:17:35,250 --> 00:17:36,790
Any nerves, going into the semis?
进半决赛了 紧张吗？

386
00:17:36,810 --> 00:17:39,860
Nerves? Against Kletzki? No. You kidding me?
紧张？对阵克莱茨基？别闹了

387
00:17:40,010 --> 00:17:42,140
Well, he's won the tournament for the last three years.
他曾连续三年夺冠

388
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:44,940
- He's got quite the reputation. - I have quite the reputation.
- 他名气可不小 - 我名气也不小

389
00:17:44,960 --> 00:17:48,850
Look, I'm gonna do to Kletzki what Auschwitz couldn't.
奥斯维辛集中营都办不到的事 我要办成

390
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:51,030
Okay. I'm gonna finish the job.
看我怎么把他灭了

391
00:17:48,860 --> 00:17:53,070
{\an8}【奥斯维辛:纳粹设立的集中营 实施种族灭绝】

392
00:17:53,090 --> 00:17:55,580
- Jesus Christ. - A little strong, mate.
- 天呐 - 这话有点过了

393
00:17:55,600 --> 00:17:57,380
It's all right. I'm Jewish. I can say that.
没事的 我能说 我也是犹太人

394
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:59,900
In fact, if you think about it, I'm like Hitler's worst nightmare.
事实上你想想 我更像是希特勒的大噩梦

395
00:17:59,910 --> 00:18:01,020
And why's that?
此话怎讲？

396
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:02,910
Look at me. I'm here.
看看我 我活得好好的

397
00:18:02,920 --> 00:18:06,900
I did it, I'm on top. I'm the ultimate product of Hitler's defeat.
还混到了上层 我就是希特勒失败的最终证明

398
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:09,580
Yeah, write that down. That was good. Write that down.
对 把这句话记下来 都记下来

399
00:18:09,590 --> 00:18:11,340
- Nice one. - "Ultimate product of Hitler's defeat."
- 不错 - “希特勒失败的最终证明”

400
00:18:11,360 --> 00:18:13,510
- Do you like that confidence? - Put that under a picture of me.
- 你总是那么自信吗？ -一定把那这句放在我照片下面

401
00:18:13,530 --> 00:18:15,950
- Tell us a bit about your background. - My background?
- 来谈谈你的出身吧 - 我的出身？

402
00:18:20,090 --> 00:18:22,970
No, but seriously... My my my mother died in childbirth.
不过说真的 我...我妈死于难产

403
00:18:22,980 --> 00:18:25,760
My father was a compulsive loser who abandoned me when I was two years old.
我爸就是个没出息的人 我两岁时他就丢下我走了

404
00:18:25,770 --> 00:18:27,520
I got stuck in the New York City orphanage system,
我被纽约孤儿院来回折腾

405
00:18:27,540 --> 00:18:29,470
got shuttled from one hellhole to the next.
到处被赶来赶去

406
00:18:29,480 --> 00:18:31,220
- Naturally, got in trouble with the law. - Isn't that Kay Stone?
- 难免有了案底 - 那不是凯·斯通吗？

407
00:18:31,240 --> 00:18:32,720
I don't want any of that to define me.
那破事可不能定义我

408
00:18:32,730 --> 00:18:34,700
Excuse me. Excuse me. What?
采访呢 采访呢 看什么呢？

409
00:18:34,720 --> 00:18:36,690
- It's Kay Stone over there. - That's her.
- 看凯·斯通 - 就是她

410
00:18:36,700 --> 00:18:37,570
Who's that?
谁？

411
00:18:37,580 --> 00:18:40,160
Well, you know, the movie actress. Like, from the 1930s.
三十年代那阵儿的老牌女星

412
00:18:40,500 --> 00:18:42,200
- Opportunities. - Opportunities?
- 演《机缘巧合》的那个 - 《机缘巧合》?

413
00:18:42,210 --> 00:18:43,700
- That was good. - Yeah, yeah. Great movie.
- 演得很好 - 是啊 佳片一个

414
00:18:43,710 --> 00:18:44,990
- Black Box. - My dad loved her.
- 还有《黑匣子》 - 我爸特喜欢她

415
00:18:45,010 --> 00:18:46,040
- Yeah. - Yeah.
- 是啊 - 没错

416
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:47,940
- She was big? - She was huge.
- 她当年很红吗？ - 红透半边天

417
00:18:47,950 --> 00:18:49,590
Came and went. That's her.
后来销声匿迹了

418
00:18:49,600 --> 00:18:52,770
- That's Hollywood, mate. - Yeah. It's her.
- 好莱坞就是这样 - 真是她

419
00:18:53,550 --> 00:18:54,630
It is indeed.
确实是她

420
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:56,420
Something about a lake?
还有个什么湖的电影

421
00:18:56,430 --> 00:18:58,930
- Shadow Lake. - Yeah, that was good.
- 《影湖》 - 嗯 那片也不错

422
00:18:59,250 --> 00:19:00,320
- Pretty. - Great legs.
- 漂亮 - 腿不错

423
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:02,140
Gorgeous, mate. Gorgeous.
太漂亮了 太漂亮了

424
00:19:02,310 --> 00:19:04,000
- Think I have a chance, lads? - No.
- 她是在看我吗？ - 不是

425
00:19:04,020 --> 00:19:05,130
I think she's looking Mauser.
她肯定在看毛瑟

426
00:19:05,150 --> 00:19:06,230
Next question.
好了 下个问题

427
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:17,020
Hello?
喂

428
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:18,700
- Kay? - Speaking.
- 凯吗？ - 有事吗？

429
00:19:18,710 --> 00:19:21,280
Hey, it's Marty Mauser. I'm in the Royal Suite.
嘿 我是马蒂·毛瑟 我住在皇家套房

430
00:19:21,290 --> 00:19:23,150
I saw you in the lobby yesterday.
我昨天在大堂见过你

431
00:19:23,160 --> 00:19:23,860
Okay.
怎么了？

432
00:19:23,880 --> 00:19:26,570
Yeah, we made eye contact. I was being interviewed.
我们互相看了一眼 当时我在接受采访

433
00:19:27,520 --> 00:19:29,700
- I don't recall. - Well...
- 我不记得了 - 这么说吧

434
00:19:30,450 --> 00:19:31,690
I'm a huge admirer.
我非常仰慕您

435
00:19:31,700 --> 00:19:33,300
Okay. Can I help you with something?
那好吧 要是没事我就挂了

436
00:19:33,320 --> 00:19:36,220
Maybe. I just ordered one of everything off the room service menu.
有点事 我刚把客房餐单上每样都点了一份

437
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:38,510
There's no way I'll be able to eat it all alone.
我一个人肯定吃不完

438
00:19:38,530 --> 00:19:39,710
Ah.
我懂了

439
00:19:39,870 --> 00:19:41,470
So you'd like me to come up to your room?
所以你想让我去你房间？

440
00:19:41,490 --> 00:19:44,350
- Mm-hmm. Yeah. - Perhaps I should send my husband instead.
- 嗯 没错 - 要不我派我丈夫去吧

441
00:19:44,360 --> 00:19:46,180
Sure. He can come up here, and I'll come down to you.
好啊 他来这里 我去你那里

442
00:19:46,190 --> 00:19:49,100
- Okay, wonderful. Thank you. Goodbye. - Wait. I wanna keep talking.
- 真一套套的 行了 再见 - 等等 我还想再说会儿

443
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:50,480
Why is that?
说什么？

444
00:19:50,500 --> 00:19:52,310
Because I've never talked to an actual movie star.
我从没跟真正的电影明星说过话

445
00:19:52,320 --> 00:19:55,400
Well, now you have. I hope the experience was all you thought it would be.
现在你说过了 希望你如愿以偿了

446
00:19:55,420 --> 00:19:57,140
You know, I'm something of a performer too.
我其实也喜欢当焦点

447
00:19:57,160 --> 00:19:59,390
- Are you? - Yeah. You don't believe me?
- 是吗？ - 是啊 你不信吗？

448
00:19:59,740 --> 00:20:01,080
I...
我...

449
00:20:01,200 --> 00:20:02,960
You... What? What?
你怎么？怎么了嘛？

450
00:20:03,680 --> 00:20:04,650
You're a performer?
你会演戏？

451
00:20:04,660 --> 00:20:07,250
Yeah, I am a performer. You got the Daily Mailin front of you?
对 会演 你手边有《每日邮报》吗？

452
00:20:07,270 --> 00:20:09,410
Uh, I do have it. Yes?
还真有 怎么了？

453
00:20:09,430 --> 00:20:11,290
Okay. Well, turn to page 12.
好的 那你翻到第12页

454
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:15,150
Uh...
等下

455
00:20:15,630 --> 00:20:16,760
Page 12.
第12页

456
00:20:16,780 --> 00:20:18,830
Okay. What am I looking at here?
好了 看什么？

457
00:20:18,840 --> 00:20:20,590
Down the middle, in the center.
看中间 正中间

458
00:20:21,530 --> 00:20:22,620
This is you?
那人是你？

459
00:20:22,630 --> 00:20:25,010
Yeah, "the chosen one." It's a nice picture, right?
对“天选之子” 拍得不错吧？

460
00:20:25,020 --> 00:20:26,100
Ping pong?
打小乒乓的？

461
00:20:25,150 --> 00:20:28,330
{\an8}（真是天选之子？）

462
00:20:26,120 --> 00:20:28,310
I play table tennis. I'm here competing in the British Open.
我打的是桌球 来这儿参加英国公开赛

463
00:20:28,330 --> 00:20:30,260
- How old are you? - I'm 23.
- 你多大了？ - 我23

464
00:20:30,270 --> 00:20:31,680
Twenty-three.
才23岁

465
00:20:31,690 --> 00:20:32,890
Yeah.
嗯

466
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:35,650
I bet you can't name one film I've done.
我赌你都说不上来我演过什么吧

467
00:20:35,670 --> 00:20:36,820
What makes you say that?
凭啥这么肯定？

468
00:20:36,840 --> 00:20:38,660
Because I stopped acting before you were born.
因为我在你出生前就不演了

469
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:40,480
- Really? That's really interesting. - Mm-hmm.
- 是吗？有点意思 - 嗯

470
00:20:40,490 --> 00:20:43,470
Kay, did you use my razor to shave your legs?
凯 你拿我的刮胡刀刮腿毛了吗？

471
00:20:43,480 --> 00:20:45,060
- It's dull. I've cut myself. - No.
- 刀钝了 我都划伤了 - 没拿

472
00:20:45,070 --> 00:20:46,490
- Who's that? Your husband? - Mm-hmm.
- 谁在说话？你丈夫？ - 嗯

473
00:20:46,500 --> 00:20:48,580
I guess someone must've snuck in and chopped wood with it.
难不成还有人偷偷溜进来用过它？

474
00:20:48,590 --> 00:20:49,870
- I'm on the phone. - Holy shit.
- 我正打电话呢 - 天呐

475
00:20:49,890 --> 00:20:51,630
- With whom? - Debbie.
- 跟谁打？ - 黛比

476
00:20:51,650 --> 00:20:53,000
- Debbie. - Debbie?
- 黛比 - 黛比？

477
00:20:53,020 --> 00:20:54,200
Tell her to get a life.
叫她少管闲事

478
00:20:54,210 --> 00:20:55,670
- Is he gone? - Mm-hmm.
- 他走了吗？ - 嗯

479
00:20:55,690 --> 00:20:57,010
Okay.
行

480
00:20:57,030 --> 00:20:59,020
So, why'd you stop acting? Let's talk about that.
那你为啥不演了？说说吧

481
00:20:59,040 --> 00:21:00,410
You know, I really have to go.
我还有事 我得挂了

482
00:21:00,430 --> 00:21:02,760
You must miss it, don't you? Come watch me play at Wembley tomorrow.
明天来温布利看我打球吧 你肯定会喜欢的

483
00:21:02,770 --> 00:21:03,780
I... I can't.
我...我去不了

484
00:21:03,800 --> 00:21:06,470
Come on. You can watch me dethrone the number one ranked player in the world.
来吧 看看我怎么战胜世界第一

485
00:21:06,480 --> 00:21:07,550
I'm not available.
我没空

486
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:08,890
Oh, yeah? What you got going on?
哦哟？你能有什么事？

487
00:21:08,910 --> 00:21:12,270
Actually, I have a big promotional event to attend to for my husband.
有个大宣传会 我得陪我丈夫撑场子

488
00:21:12,290 --> 00:21:13,890
Oh, okay.
哦 好吧

489
00:21:13,910 --> 00:21:15,410
What's he promoting?
宣传什么？

490
00:21:15,430 --> 00:21:16,560
Pens.
笔

491
00:21:16,890 --> 00:21:18,680
- Pens? Are you serious? - Pens.
- 卖笔？开什么玩笑 - 就是笔

492
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:20,490
- Like, writing pens? - Yes.
- 写字用的笔？ - 对

493
00:21:20,500 --> 00:21:22,340
What, like, he's a pen salesman?
他就是个卖笔的？

494
00:21:22,900 --> 00:21:24,500
How can you afford the suite you're in?
你们怎么住得起这种套房？

495
00:21:24,520 --> 00:21:26,570
He owns Rockwell Ink.
他是罗克韦尔墨业的老板

496
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:27,820
Oh. Okay. Well...
哦 那好吧...

497
00:21:27,830 --> 00:21:28,830
Yes.
是的

498
00:21:29,060 --> 00:21:31,280
- I know Rockwell Ink. - I'm sure you do.
- 我听说过罗克韦尔墨业 - 你肯定知道

499
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:32,330
Okay.
好吧

500
00:21:32,860 --> 00:21:34,530
Well, what's the event?
那活动内容是什么？

501
00:21:34,550 --> 00:21:38,750
He's hired Agatha Christie to sign books at Hatchards.
他请了阿加莎·克里斯蒂去哈查兹书店签名售书

502
00:21:34,550 --> 00:21:39,780
{\an8}【阿加莎·克里斯蒂为英国知名小说家 哈查兹为伦敦老牌书店】

503
00:21:38,760 --> 00:21:39,830
Ooh.
哦 哦

504
00:21:40,750 --> 00:21:42,040
That sounds really boring.
听着就无聊

505
00:21:42,060 --> 00:21:43,160
Okay.
行了

506
00:21:52,040 --> 00:21:54,660
Oh, for God's sake.
哦 没完没了了

507
00:21:56,200 --> 00:21:58,310
- What is it? - Don't hang up, don't hang up. Just one question.
- 有完没完？ - 别挂 别挂 问你个事

508
00:21:58,320 --> 00:22:00,070
Does your room face the street or the courtyard?
你房间是朝街还是朝院子？

509
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:01,070
I don't know.
不知道

510
00:22:01,090 --> 00:22:03,160
Just answer the question. Is it facing the street or the courtyard?
直说 朝街还是院子？

511
00:22:03,180 --> 00:22:04,570
- The courtyard. - Okay.
- 朝院子 - 好

512
00:22:04,580 --> 00:22:06,120
I need you to go to the window.
去窗边看看

513
00:22:06,130 --> 00:22:07,460
What floor are you on?
你住几楼？

514
00:22:07,470 --> 00:22:09,040
I'm on the third floor, I believe.
三楼吧

515
00:22:09,060 --> 00:22:10,700
Third floor. Okay, perfect.
三楼 好 正好

516
00:22:10,710 --> 00:22:11,670
Look across the street.
朝对面看看

517
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:14,470
You see the open window with a bowl of fruit on the table?
看见对面那开窗 桌上有果盘的屋了吗？

518
00:22:15,750 --> 00:22:17,730
- You see it? - I do.
- 看到了吗？ - 看到了

519
00:22:17,750 --> 00:22:21,000
Here's what's gonna happen. I'm gonna make an apple appear in that bowl.
看好了 我会让那果盘里凭空多出一个苹果

520
00:22:21,010 --> 00:22:23,650
And if I do, you're gonna blow off your little rendezvous
要是我办到了 你就推掉你那场会

521
00:22:23,670 --> 00:22:25,240
- No, no, no. - and come watch me play.
- 不 不 不 - 来看我比赛

522
00:22:25,250 --> 00:22:26,840
I'm not agreeing to anything, no.
我不会答应任何事

523
00:22:26,850 --> 00:22:28,700
You don't have to agree to anything. I'm gonna do it anyway.
你不用答应 但看好了

524
00:22:28,710 --> 00:22:29,820
Okay? One...
看到了 一

525
00:22:30,690 --> 00:22:31,700
two...
二

526
00:22:32,340 --> 00:22:33,480
three.
三

527
00:22:37,090 --> 00:22:39,510
I'll leave a ticket for you at the box office.
票我留售票处 你去取

528
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:07,560
{\an8}（半决赛）

529
00:23:15,810 --> 00:23:19,490
Mauser. Nineteen to five
马蒂·毛瑟 19比5

530
00:23:29,320 --> 00:23:30,950
Point, Mauser.
马蒂·毛瑟 得分

531
00:23:30,970 --> 00:23:33,200
Twenty to five.
20比5

532
00:23:33,220 --> 00:23:36,830
Kletzki trails Mauser two games to nil.
克莱茨基整场落后两局 零局比二

533
00:23:37,250 --> 00:23:40,410
Game and match point, Mauser.
马蒂·毛瑟 局点兼赛点

534
00:23:37,250 --> 00:23:40,420
{\an8}【局点兼赛点:表示马蒂再得一分即可赢下整场比赛】

535
00:23:40,430 --> 00:23:42,160
- Let's have a little fun with this one. - Okay.
- 咱们找点乐子玩玩 - 好吧

536
00:23:42,170 --> 00:23:43,710
- Have a little fun, all right? - Gotcha.
- 玩出花样来 - 收到

537
00:23:44,290 --> 00:23:46,190
Service switches to Kletzki.
换克莱茨基发球

538
00:24:16,790 --> 00:24:18,460
Point, Kletzki.
克莱茨基 得分

539
00:24:24,010 --> 00:24:26,360
Very well, gentlemen. Thank you for that. Thank you.
好的 诸位 谢谢大家 谢谢大家

540
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:33,140
Kletzki serves 6-20.
克莱茨基发球 当前局分6比20

541
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:36,850
Mauser leads two games to zero.
马蒂·毛瑟整场领先两局 两局比零

542
00:24:36,860 --> 00:24:38,690
Match point again for Mr. Mauser.
又是马蒂·毛瑟的赛点

543
00:24:38,710 --> 00:24:40,670
Your service again, Kletzki.
再次由你发球 克莱茨基

544
00:24:45,070 --> 00:24:46,720
Point, Mauser!
马蒂·毛瑟 得分

545
00:24:48,390 --> 00:24:52,680
Mauser wins the game and match by 21-6. Three games to nil.
马蒂·毛瑟以21比6赢下此局 以三局比零赢下整场比赛

546
00:24:52,690 --> 00:24:57,640
Mauser's on to the finals where he will face Koto Endo of Japan.
马蒂·毛瑟进入决赛 将对阵日本选手远藤功人

547
00:25:00,560 --> 00:25:03,740
{\an8}（菜单）

548
00:25:01,670 --> 00:25:03,790
Get whatever you want. Don't even look at the prices, okay?
别去看价钱 想吃什么随便点

549
00:25:04,010 --> 00:25:04,880
What are you getting?
你点什么？

550
00:25:04,900 --> 00:25:07,470
I'm gonna get the Beef Wellington and the caviar tasting plate
我就来个威灵顿牛排和鱼子酱拼盘

551
00:25:07,490 --> 00:25:09,340
because they're the most expensive items on the menu.
要点就点最贵的

552
00:25:09,360 --> 00:25:12,340
Listen, I would like to keep going back a little bit about the Globetrotters.
我想再唠叨两句关于巡回表演队的事

553
00:25:12,350 --> 00:25:13,930
- About the Harlem Globetrotters, again? - Yes.
- 哈林篮球队那事儿？ - 对

554
00:25:12,350 --> 00:25:16,700
{\an8}【哈林篮球队:美国巡回表演篮球队 擅长花式竞技与表演】

555
00:25:13,950 --> 00:25:15,470
- I told you, I'm not interested. - Why not?
- 我跟你说过了 我不干 - 为什么？

556
00:25:15,490 --> 00:25:16,680
'Cause I don't wanna do it.
就是不想干

557
00:25:16,700 --> 00:25:18,390
It's great money.
报酬很高

558
00:25:18,400 --> 00:25:20,790
And we will travel all over the world. Have you seen Venice?
咱们还能环游世界 你不想去威尼斯吗？

559
00:25:20,810 --> 00:25:22,810
- I don't wanna be doing trick shots for a halftime show - Sydney?
- 我才不会去当马戏团的中场把戏 - 悉尼呢？

560
00:25:22,830 --> 00:25:24,440
- while people are going to the bathroom. - Barcelona?
- 观众上厕所时上场 - 巴塞罗那？

561
00:25:24,460 --> 00:25:25,530
That's beneath me, okay?
真丢人 明白吗？

562
00:25:25,550 --> 00:25:28,570
- They're treated like royalty. - Where's the waiter?
- 观众相当捧他们的 - 服务员在哪儿呢？

563
00:25:28,590 --> 00:25:31,100
- Listen, I know people who have done this. - Excuse me.
- 我有个熟人干过这行 - 服务员

564
00:25:31,110 --> 00:25:32,390
Excuse me.
服务员

565
00:25:32,410 --> 00:25:35,600
It's a great opportunity. We should not miss it.
机会难得 咱们得把握住

566
00:25:38,270 --> 00:25:39,520
Marty.
马蒂

567
00:25:41,680 --> 00:25:43,180
Yes, sir. May I help you, sir?
先生 请问需要帮助吗？

568
00:25:43,190 --> 00:25:44,260
Hi. Can we order?
可以点菜了吗？

569
00:25:44,270 --> 00:25:45,710
Of course, sir. Let me fetch your waiter.
没问题 我马上去叫这桌的服务员来

570
00:25:45,730 --> 00:25:47,030
- Hang on. - Yes.
- 别走 - 请说

571
00:25:47,260 --> 00:25:49,330
Uh, I'll be taking care of the Rockwell tab tonight.
今晚罗克韦尔的账由我来结

572
00:25:49,340 --> 00:25:52,140
Put it on my room. The Royal Suite. Marty Mauser.
把账记我房间上 皇家套房 马蒂·毛瑟

573
00:25:52,160 --> 00:25:54,400
- And make sure they know it's me, too. - I will. Leave it to me, sir.
- 跟他们交代清楚 是我付的账 - 明白 先生

574
00:25:54,410 --> 00:25:55,930
- Don't take no for an answer. - I won't.
- 不许被回绝 - 没问题

575
00:25:55,950 --> 00:25:58,930
- Marty Mauser. Royal Suite. Go tell 'em. - Will do, sir.
- 马蒂·毛瑟 皇家套房 去告诉他们 - 好的 先生

576
00:26:01,270 --> 00:26:03,390
Okay. Look at me. Don't look there. Look at me.
行了 看着我 别往那儿瞅 看着我

577
00:26:03,400 --> 00:26:04,890
- Who's Rockwell? - Some bozo.
- 罗克韦尔是谁啊 - 就个傻瓜

578
00:26:04,900 --> 00:26:07,270
Look over now. Be subtle about it. What's he doing?
现在看过去 别太明显 告诉我他在干啥？

579
00:26:08,150 --> 00:26:10,020
He hasn't been here before, sir.
抱歉先生 他之前没来过我们酒店

580
00:26:10,030 --> 00:26:11,020
He's looking at us.
他在看这边

581
00:26:11,040 --> 00:26:12,100
- Really? - Yeah.
- 是吗？ - 嗯

582
00:26:12,120 --> 00:26:13,610
Okay, keep talking to me. Be normal.
好 继续跟我说话 别露馅

583
00:26:13,620 --> 00:26:15,650
Okay, fine. I want you to reconsider.
好吧 听我说 再考虑一下

584
00:26:15,660 --> 00:26:17,440
We would be a great team. I wanna do this with you.
我们会是绝佳组合 我想跟你搭档

585
00:26:17,450 --> 00:26:19,360
Why are you so fixed on the Harlem Globetrotters?
干嘛老想着哈林篮球队？

586
00:26:19,370 --> 00:26:21,410
It's very sad what they do, okay?
那群人干的真丢人

587
00:26:21,430 --> 00:26:24,600
Some of the premier athletes on the planet reduced to acting like circus clowns.
本该是顶尖的运动员却成了杂耍的小丑

588
00:26:24,610 --> 00:26:25,980
What's he doing now?
再看看什么情况

589
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:27,340
- He's coming towards us. - He's coming?
- 他正朝这桌走来 - 他来了？

590
00:26:27,360 --> 00:26:30,300
- Just be normal. Act casual. - Okay, fine. Okay.
- 别紧张 表现得自然点 - 行 好的 明白

591
00:26:34,390 --> 00:26:36,580
Excuse me. Do I know you?
劳驾 我认识你吗？

592
00:26:37,410 --> 00:26:38,600
I don't think so.
应该不认识

593
00:26:38,620 --> 00:26:40,890
And you wanna buy dinner for my entire table tonight?
你居然想请客？

594
00:26:40,910 --> 00:26:43,140
- Yeah. Is it okay? - Why?
- 对 可以吗？ - 为什么？

595
00:26:43,390 --> 00:26:44,810
What do you mean, why? Do I need a reason?
什么叫为什么？我还需要理由？

596
00:26:44,820 --> 00:26:47,230
Let me rephrase that. What do you want?
我换个说法 你图什么？

597
00:26:47,240 --> 00:26:50,180
No, I don't want anything. It's just my small way of saying thank you.
不 我什么都不图 只是想表示点谢意

598
00:26:50,190 --> 00:26:51,950
- Thank you? - Yeah.
- 谢我？ - 对

599
00:26:51,970 --> 00:26:53,380
Thank me for what, specifically?
具体谢我什么？

600
00:26:53,390 --> 00:26:54,960
For all your products.
谢谢您那些产品

601
00:26:54,970 --> 00:26:57,720
I mean, where would we be without pens?
没了你们的笔 世界该怎么办？

602
00:26:59,450 --> 00:27:01,860
You know, I have many talents, but the one I'm most proud of
你看 我有不少本事 但最得意的就是

603
00:27:01,870 --> 00:27:04,840
- is the ability to smell bullshit from a mile away. - No,
- 能大老远闻出屁话 - 不

604
00:27:04,850 --> 00:27:07,150
I'm being completely sincere.
我说的都是真心话

605
00:27:09,760 --> 00:27:12,220
- Where are you from? - New York. What about you?
- 你是哪儿人？ - 纽约人 你呢？

606
00:27:12,230 --> 00:27:14,010
New York too. What do you do?
也是纽约 你是做什么的？

607
00:27:14,020 --> 00:27:15,500
I'm a professional athlete.
我是个职业运动员

608
00:27:15,510 --> 00:27:17,600
- Really? What sport? - Table tennis.
- 真的吗 哪项运动？ - 桌上网球

609
00:27:17,620 --> 00:27:19,060
Table tennis? That's a sport?
桌球？这也算运动？

610
00:27:19,070 --> 00:27:20,980
Of course it is. I'm here competing in the British Open.
当然算 我来参加英国公开赛的

611
00:27:20,990 --> 00:27:22,300
I'm playing at Wembley tomorrow
我明天要在温布利打决赛

612
00:27:22,310 --> 00:27:24,190
in front of a sold-out crowd in the finals against Japan.
对阵日本 明天赛场座无虚席

613
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:25,480
- I'm here representing the United States. - Wait, wait, wait.
- 我代表美国出赛 - 等一下

614
00:27:25,500 --> 00:27:28,090
Japan? Japan has a team here?
日本？日本也来了？

615
00:27:28,100 --> 00:27:30,190
- That's what I just said. - How'd they get around the travel ban?
- 我刚才不是说了吗 - 那出境管制呢？

616
00:27:30,210 --> 00:27:32,500
Because table tennis is the fastest growing sport in Asia.
因为桌球在亚洲增长最快

617
00:27:32,510 --> 00:27:34,180
It's huge over there.
在那边火得不行

618
00:27:34,190 --> 00:27:35,200
Oh, you're gonna like this.
说个有意思的事

619
00:27:35,220 --> 00:27:37,620
Do you know what they call their grip? The way they hold their rackets?
你知道他们怎么握拍的吗？

620
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:39,580
- No. - They call it penholder.
- 不知道 - 他们管那叫直笔握拍

621
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:40,890
{\an8}【直拍:起源日本 英文含“握笔”之意】

622
00:27:40,910 --> 00:27:41,700
So what?
那又怎样？

623
00:27:41,720 --> 00:27:43,070
You can use that.
你可以拿去用

624
00:27:43,080 --> 00:27:44,040
Use it for what?
用来干嘛？

625
00:27:44,050 --> 00:27:47,280
For an advertisement or something. I don't know, you're the business guy.
拿去当宣传素材 我哪知道 我又不是生意人

626
00:27:47,290 --> 00:27:49,490
I'm being rude. This is my associate, Béla Kletzki.
刚才有点失礼 这位是我搭档贝拉·克莱茨基

627
00:27:49,500 --> 00:27:50,670
Nice to meet you, sir.
幸会 先生

628
00:27:50,690 --> 00:27:52,880
I assume you're a table tennis player also?
你也是打桌球的？

629
00:27:52,900 --> 00:27:56,520
I am. I am. Actually, I was the World Champion from '35 to '39.
是的 没错 我是1935到39年的世界冠军

630
00:27:56,530 --> 00:27:58,170
He was the World Champion. I beat him today.
前世界冠军 我今天把他打败了

631
00:27:58,190 --> 00:27:59,890
He beat me. But he's much younger than me.
他赢了我 他比我年轻得多

632
00:27:59,910 --> 00:28:01,630
I'm much better than him, much more talented.
也强得多 更有天赋

633
00:28:01,640 --> 00:28:05,860
I can't help but notice this tattoo. You were in one of the camps, weren't you?
我看到这个纹身 你是不是进过集中营？

634
00:28:05,880 --> 00:28:08,400
Auschwitz-Birkenau. Yeah. Why do you ask?
奥斯威辛二号营区 没错 怎么问这个？

635
00:28:08,410 --> 00:28:10,920
My son lost his life liberating you.
我儿子为了解放你们付出了生命

636
00:28:13,070 --> 00:28:14,990
I'm sorry for your loss.
我深表遗憾

637
00:28:15,400 --> 00:28:17,230
I thought you were liberated by the Soviets.
我还以为是苏联人解放你们的

638
00:28:17,240 --> 00:28:18,790
- We were. It's Soviets. - It wasn't the Americans.
- 确实是 是苏联 - 并不是美国人

639
00:28:18,810 --> 00:28:21,680
I didn't mean it literally. He was serving in the South Pacific.
不是字面意思 我儿子在太平洋战场

640
00:28:21,700 --> 00:28:23,920
Well, what happened to him?
那他后来怎么了？

641
00:28:23,930 --> 00:28:25,870
What do you mean? He was killed.
还能怎么了 他被杀了

642
00:28:26,790 --> 00:28:27,940
You find that funny?
你觉得这好笑吗？

643
00:28:27,960 --> 00:28:31,910
Oh, God. No, I just get nervous laughter sometimes.
天呐 不是 我有时一紧张就会笑

644
00:28:31,920 --> 00:28:33,130
If it's any consolation,
说句安慰话

645
00:28:33,150 --> 00:28:35,720
I'll be dropping a third atom bomb on their heads tomorrow.
我明天会送给他们第三颗原子弹

646
00:28:35,740 --> 00:28:37,750
Yeah, I'm sure his mother's gonna get a lot of comfort
你这套安慰话 顶多忽悠你妈

647
00:28:37,760 --> 00:28:39,620
that you're playing ping pong in his honor.
让她不反对你去打小乒乓

648
00:28:39,640 --> 00:28:41,800
It's not that big of a deal, but I appreciate it.
感谢您操心我家事

649
00:28:41,810 --> 00:28:44,430
Tell him-- He used to diffuse bombs for the Nazis.
跟他讲讲...他以前给纳粹拆弹

650
00:28:44,450 --> 00:28:46,180
Tell him the story you told me about--
跟他讲讲那故事

651
00:28:46,190 --> 00:28:47,910
- I've got a whole table of people waiting. - No, no, no, wait, wait.
- 我那桌还有人等我 我得走了 - 别走 别走

652
00:28:47,930 --> 00:28:49,770
You're gonna love this story. Tell him.
他会喜欢的 讲给他听

653
00:28:50,560 --> 00:28:52,650
- You wanna hear it? - Not really, but go ahead.
- 你想听吗？ - 不太想 但快说吧

654
00:28:52,670 --> 00:28:54,110
No, tell him. It's beautiful.
别停 快说 是好故事

655
00:28:54,120 --> 00:28:56,010
Okay, I'll make it quick. So...
行 那我长话短说

656
00:28:56,020 --> 00:28:59,710
when I first got to the camp, I was put into housing.
我进集中营被分配住处的时候

657
00:28:59,720 --> 00:29:02,620
Lucky for me, there was an officer who recognized me.
幸好有个军官认出我

658
00:29:02,640 --> 00:29:07,320
He had seen me in 1935 at the World Championships in Prague.
他在1935年布拉格世锦赛上见过我

659
00:29:07,330 --> 00:29:10,910
This guy was a real fan. I mean, a real fan, okay?
那人是真心崇拜我 真心的

660
00:29:10,920 --> 00:29:13,810
You're telling me he let you live because you played ping pong?
他居然因为你会打小乒乓就让你活着？

661
00:29:13,820 --> 00:29:15,870
They respected my skills, yeah.
他们很佩服我的本事 没错

662
00:29:17,370 --> 00:29:21,790
So then, they taught me how to dismantle SC bombs.
于是他们教我拆圆柱高爆炸弹

663
00:29:22,140 --> 00:29:23,220
Okay?
明白吗？

664
00:29:23,240 --> 00:29:26,810
Each morning, they would send me into the woods with the bombs
每天早上他们把我和炸弹送到营外的树林里

665
00:29:26,830 --> 00:29:30,460
on the outskirts of the camp where I could only do damage to myself.
就算炸了也伤不到别人

666
00:29:33,610 --> 00:29:35,190
So one time,
有一回

667
00:29:35,880 --> 00:29:37,570
I followed a honeybee.
我尾随一只蜜蜂

668
00:29:37,590 --> 00:29:38,730
A bee?
什么蜂？

669
00:29:38,750 --> 00:29:40,350
A honeybee,
蜜蜂

670
00:29:40,370 --> 00:29:42,390
all the way to its hive.
一路跟它到了蜂巢

671
00:29:44,900 --> 00:29:46,900
And I smoked all the bees out.
然后我用烟把蜜蜂全都熏跑

672
00:29:47,990 --> 00:29:50,510
And then broke it open,
接着我把巢掰开

673
00:29:50,520 --> 00:29:54,690
and I smeared the honey all over my chest, my arms, everywhere.
我把蜂蜜抹满全身 胸口 胳膊全抹上了

674
00:29:55,000 --> 00:29:56,090
Why?
为什么？

675
00:29:56,110 --> 00:29:57,890
'Cause later that night,
晚上回去后

676
00:29:57,900 --> 00:30:02,560
I let all my bunk mates to lick the honey off of me for nourishment.
我就让室友把我身上的蜜舔掉充饥

677
00:30:20,240 --> 00:30:31,040
{\an8}（皇家套房）

678
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:45,440
Heads.
押正面

679
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:50,700
{\an8}【抛硬币猜中者先选“发球”或“场地” 二选一】

680
00:31:47,640 --> 00:31:49,220
- Fuck. - Endo, choice?
- 真倒霉 - 远藤 轮到你选了

681
00:31:49,230 --> 00:31:50,690
（日语）发球

682
00:31:50,710 --> 00:31:52,210
I'll go to that side.
我选那边

683
00:31:56,460 --> 00:31:59,680
{\an8}（决赛）

684
00:31:58,880 --> 00:32:00,960
- On my right... - Come on, Marty! Come on!
- 右侧... - 加油 马蒂 加油

685
00:32:00,980 --> 00:32:04,740
...Marty Mauser of the United States, ranked second,
是美国选手马蒂·毛瑟 世界排名第二

686
00:32:04,760 --> 00:32:09,310
versus Koto Endo of Japan, unranked.
对阵日本选手远藤功人 未列排名

687
00:32:09,330 --> 00:32:12,390
The gentlemen will battle to the best of five
比赛为五局三胜

688
00:32:12,400 --> 00:32:14,710
in games to 21 points.
单局21分制

689
00:32:15,410 --> 00:32:18,720
Each game shall be won by at least two points.
每局须至少领先两分才能取胜

690
00:32:19,820 --> 00:32:21,030
Good luck, gentlemen.
祝二位好运

691
00:32:19,960 --> 00:32:23,430
{\an8}（第一局）

692
00:32:22,050 --> 00:32:23,470
Quiet, please.
请保持安静

693
00:32:24,890 --> 00:32:26,430
All right!
比赛开始

694
00:32:33,970 --> 00:32:37,960
Point, Endo. One-nil.
远藤 得分 1比0

695
00:32:42,540 --> 00:32:44,420
Come on, America!
加油 美国人

696
00:32:47,360 --> 00:32:51,490
Point, Endo. Two-nil.
远藤 得分 2比0

697
00:32:53,770 --> 00:32:55,100
All right, Marty!
加油 马蒂

698
00:32:56,730 --> 00:32:57,940
Come on, Marty!
加油啊 马蒂

699
00:33:00,640 --> 00:33:03,640
Point, Endo. Three-nil.
远藤 得分 3比0

700
00:33:13,270 --> 00:33:17,190
Point, Endo. Four-nil.
远藤 得分 4比0

701
00:33:22,520 --> 00:33:24,100
Come on, Marty!
加油 马蒂

702
00:33:30,090 --> 00:33:33,930
Point, Endo. Five-nil.
远藤 得分 5比0

703
00:33:36,060 --> 00:33:38,500
Service switches to Mauser.
换马蒂·毛瑟发球

704
00:33:42,040 --> 00:33:44,390
{\an8}（局分:美国8比日本19 场分:美国零比一）

705
00:33:43,520 --> 00:33:46,110
Point, Mauser.
马蒂·毛瑟 得分

706
00:33:44,390 --> 00:33:46,340
{\an8}（局分:美国9比日本19 场分:美国零比一）

707
00:33:46,120 --> 00:33:48,790
Nine serving 19.
9比19 美方发球

708
00:33:51,010 --> 00:33:53,760
{\an8}（第二局）

709
00:34:05,210 --> 00:34:09,470
Point, Mauser. 10-19.
马蒂·毛瑟 得分 10比19

710
00:34:09,490 --> 00:34:10,570
Okay, Marty!
好样的 马蒂

711
00:34:34,990 --> 00:34:38,950
Point, Endo. 20-10.
远藤 得分 20比10

712
00:34:40,160 --> 00:34:45,420
{\an8}【局点:率先达到者只需再得一分即可赢此局】

713
00:34:40,160 --> 00:34:41,870
Game point.
局点

714
00:34:45,950 --> 00:34:47,460
Go! Serve.
快发球

715
00:35:07,860 --> 00:35:11,860
Point, Endo. 21-10.
远藤 得分 21比10

716
00:35:11,880 --> 00:35:13,820
Game, Endo.
本局远藤胜

717
00:35:14,560 --> 00:35:19,020
Endo leads two games to zero.
远藤以两局比零领先

718
00:35:20,830 --> 00:35:23,390
{\an8}（局分:美国16比日本18 场分:美国零比二）

719
00:35:21,510 --> 00:35:23,830
Point, Mauser.
马蒂·毛瑟 得分

720
00:35:23,850 --> 00:35:26,180
Eighteen-16.
18比16

721
00:35:26,710 --> 00:35:28,630
{\an8}(第三局)

722
00:35:40,100 --> 00:35:44,270
Point, Mauser. 17-18.
马蒂·毛瑟 得分 17比18

723
00:35:44,290 --> 00:35:45,570
Go, Marty! Come on!
加油 马蒂 加油

724
00:35:45,580 --> 00:35:48,250
Service switches to Mauser.
换马蒂·毛瑟发球

725
00:36:01,700 --> 00:36:03,540
Fuck.
该死

726
00:36:07,460 --> 00:36:11,170
Point, Endo. 17-19.
远藤 得分 17比19

727
00:36:26,860 --> 00:36:28,010
Oh, fuck.
真见鬼了

728
00:36:30,900 --> 00:36:35,640
Point, Endo. 17-20.
远藤 得分 17比20

729
00:36:35,660 --> 00:36:37,430
And match point.
赛点

730
00:36:44,070 --> 00:36:46,030
Quiet, please.
请安静

731
00:36:46,620 --> 00:36:49,130
Quiet. Settle down.
请坐好 保持安静

732
00:36:50,130 --> 00:36:51,870
Your service, Mauser.
马蒂·毛瑟发球

733
00:36:51,880 --> 00:36:54,020
Come on, Marty!
加油啊 马蒂

734
00:37:02,010 --> 00:37:03,270
Fuck.
完了

735
00:37:04,730 --> 00:37:06,640
No, bullshit! No!
不行 这是胡闹 不行

736
00:37:06,660 --> 00:37:09,310
I want a rematch right now with a standard-league hard-bat!
现在就给我重赛 用正规硬拍

737
00:37:06,660 --> 00:37:14,230
{\an8}【1952年孟买世锦赛 日本选手佐藤博治首次用海绵拍 并赢得男单冠军】

738
00:37:09,330 --> 00:37:10,510
That is unacceptable!
这太不像话了

739
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:12,240
What if I had a mechanical arm?
要是我装了机械臂呢？

740
00:37:12,250 --> 00:37:14,250
What if I put glue on the ball? Would that be kosher?
要是我在球上涂胶水呢？这合规吗？

741
00:37:14,270 --> 00:37:17,440
Why, he was getting coached the entire time! That is unacceptable!
他全场都被教练指点 这太不像话

742
00:37:19,450 --> 00:37:22,800
I play real table tennis! Real table tennis!
我打的可是正经桌球 正经桌球

743
00:37:23,560 --> 00:37:24,650
Unbelievable.
胡闹啊

744
00:37:24,990 --> 00:37:26,070
Unbelievable.
胡闹啊

745
00:37:26,080 --> 00:37:28,410
...British Open champion from Japan...
本届英国公开赛冠军是...

746
00:37:28,420 --> 00:37:29,500
Fuck you!
去死吧你

747
00:37:29,520 --> 00:37:31,860
...Koto Endo!
...日本选手远藤功人

748
00:37:34,210 --> 00:37:36,670
{\an8}（日本新闻）

749
00:37:38,290 --> 00:37:42,640
{\an8}（特别报道）

750
00:37:38,290 --> 00:37:42,180
（日语）第19届英国桌球公开赛上 日本首次问鼎冠军

751
00:37:43,550 --> 00:37:45,880
（日语）这是自太平洋战争结束以来

752
00:37:45,900 --> 00:37:49,450
（日语）首位日本选手在国际赛场上夺得胜利

753
00:37:52,140 --> 00:37:54,060
（日语）获胜者为远藤功人

754
00:37:55,820 --> 00:37:58,290
（日语）这位无名的日本挑战者 他在决赛中

755
00:37:58,310 --> 00:38:02,500
（日语）以3比0的压倒性优势击败夺冠热门的美国强手

756
00:38:08,650 --> 00:38:10,870
（日语）东京十万民众涌上街头

757
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:12,850
（日语）宛若庆典游行

758
00:38:12,860 --> 00:38:14,640
（日语）热烈欢庆他的凯旋

759
00:38:16,310 --> 00:38:20,070
（日语）远藤却以谦逊自持 愿以一名普通工匠身份回国

760
00:38:20,090 --> 00:38:22,920
（日语）而非受封为所谓英雄

761
00:38:23,020 --> 00:38:27,730
（日语）远藤16岁遭遇东京大轰炸 失去听觉

762
00:38:27,740 --> 00:38:31,380
（日语）他在无声之中磨砺感官 最终以钢铁般意志征服赛场

763
00:38:32,800 --> 00:38:36,400
（日语）如今 世界桌球的目光聚焦于我邦

764
00:38:34,680 --> 00:38:39,890
{\an8}（第23界世界桌球锦标赛）

765
00:38:36,420 --> 00:38:40,100
（日语）本年度世界锦标赛主办地已定为东京

766
00:38:40,110 --> 00:38:44,070
（日语）美国选手必将卷土重来 誓要洗刷败绩

767
00:38:44,700 --> 00:38:47,060
（日语）但远藤并非孤军奋战

768
00:38:47,070 --> 00:38:49,430
（日语）他背靠的是与他一道齐心实现民族愿望

769
00:38:49,440 --> 00:38:52,840
（日语）共怀不屈精神的八千四百万同胞

770
00:38:52,980 --> 00:38:55,750
{\an8}（完）

771
00:39:00,740 --> 00:39:03,150
{\an8}（法国 巴黎）

772
00:39:13,770 --> 00:39:15,630
Bonjour monsieur, Est‑ce que je peux vous aider?
（法语）您好先生 有什么需要吗？

773
00:39:15,640 --> 00:39:17,400
Do you have a Milton Rockwell reservation?
米尔顿·罗克韦尔订的桌子在哪儿？

774
00:39:17,420 --> 00:39:20,690
- Excusez-moi? - Milton Rockwell reservation, please.
- （法语）您说什么？ - 请查下米尔顿·罗克韦尔的订位

775
00:39:20,710 --> 00:39:21,850
Ah, Rockwell?
（法语）您是说罗克韦尔吧？

776
00:39:21,860 --> 00:39:24,130
So, listen, Marty, I wanna personally thank you
听着 马蒂 我得亲自谢谢你

777
00:39:24,140 --> 00:39:26,640
for introducing me to table tennis.
谢谢你带我接触桌球

778
00:39:27,310 --> 00:39:29,940
I had no idea what a phenomenon it was in the Asias.
我压根儿没想到 这玩意能在亚洲火成那样

779
00:39:29,950 --> 00:39:31,850
- Oh, yeah. I know. - And how big it is in Japan!
- 哦 对 对 - 尤其在日本

780
00:39:31,860 --> 00:39:33,580
That's what I was trying to tell you. It's huge.
我早跟你说了 火得很

781
00:39:33,600 --> 00:39:36,280
So, I'm thinking of incorporating it into some of the promotional events
所以 我打算把桌球列进

782
00:39:36,290 --> 00:39:38,380
we're gonna be doing over there in the fall.
秋季在那边的宣传项目里

783
00:39:38,400 --> 00:39:39,750
How so? What are you thinking?
你准备怎么安排？

784
00:39:39,770 --> 00:39:42,510
What I wanna do is stage an exhibition match
我想在世锦赛期间

785
00:39:42,530 --> 00:39:46,320
around the time of the World Championships between you and Endo.
安排一场你和远藤的表演赛

786
00:39:46,330 --> 00:39:48,260
- Mmm. - I think you'd like that idea.
- 嗯 - 你肯定会喜欢的

787
00:39:48,280 --> 00:39:49,810
So I'm gonna make you an offer.
我给你开个价

788
00:39:49,820 --> 00:39:51,690
I'll pay you a thousand dollars.
1000美金酬劳

789
00:39:49,820 --> 00:39:51,690
{\an8}【约1.2万美元 8.5万人民币 37万新台币】

790
00:39:51,700 --> 00:39:54,190
I'll put you up at the Imperial Hotel in Tokyo.
还安排你住东京帝国饭店

791
00:39:51,700 --> 00:39:54,210
{\an8}【东京帝国饭店:建于19世纪末 东京三大顶级酒店之一】

792
00:39:54,210 --> 00:39:57,010
And if you're leaving from New York, I'll give you a seat on my private plane,
要是你从纽约出发 还可以坐我的私人飞机

793
00:39:57,020 --> 00:39:59,260
and you'll fly in luxury for the first time in your life.
让你这辈子体验一回什么叫奢华

794
00:39:59,270 --> 00:40:00,650
Okay, we can negotiate my price later.
钱的事之后再商量

795
00:40:00,670 --> 00:40:02,400
But this would be before or after the tournament?
但这安排是在赛前还是赛后？

796
00:40:02,420 --> 00:40:04,200
- About a week before the event. - No, it's gotta be after.
- 赛前一周左右 - 不行 必须是赛后

797
00:40:04,220 --> 00:40:06,360
I can't face off against the guy in public before it actually counts.
我不能在紧要关头前陪他演戏

798
00:40:06,380 --> 00:40:07,890
Drama is very important to me. I can't undercut the drama.
好戏要留到关键时候

799
00:40:07,910 --> 00:40:09,310
Let's not get tied up in minutiae.
先别纠结细节

800
00:40:09,330 --> 00:40:11,470
- I just want to find out if you're interested in participating. - Yes.
- 我只是想知道你有没有兴趣参加 - 有啊

801
00:40:11,480 --> 00:40:14,150
Oh, yeah. Of course. I'm interested in any opportunity to show off my talents.
当然有 凡是能让我露一手的机会我都不会错过

802
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:16,970
And you don't have to worry either, 'cause this time I'm gonna obliterate him.
别担心 这回我一定完胜他

803
00:40:16,980 --> 00:40:18,660
It's really the racket that I'm playing,
主要是球拍的问题

804
00:40:18,670 --> 00:40:20,290
but I can assure you, it's gonna be a victory.
但我保证 准能赢

805
00:40:20,300 --> 00:40:22,500
Okay, listen. I need you to understand what this thing's about.
行了 听着 你得明白这是怎么回事

806
00:40:22,510 --> 00:40:25,080
This is not an official match.
这不是正式比赛

807
00:40:25,090 --> 00:40:26,830
It's not even a real game.
连真打都算不上

808
00:40:26,840 --> 00:40:31,010
This is purely promotional, to entertain the Japanese people,
这是纯粹的宣传 目的就是讨好日本人

809
00:40:31,030 --> 00:40:33,930
so they buy more of my pens, okay?
好让他们多买我的笔 明白吗？

810
00:40:33,950 --> 00:40:36,710
You're gonna play a few games. You're gonna be great.
你上去打几局 你会很亮眼

811
00:40:36,720 --> 00:40:39,890
- But you can't play better than Endo. - You want me to lose?
- 但别把远藤的风头给抢了 - 你让我故意输给他？

812
00:40:41,440 --> 00:40:44,250
Marty, let me show you something.
马蒂 给你看样东西

813
00:40:45,190 --> 00:40:47,520
Biggest magazine in Japan.
日本头号杂志

814
00:40:47,530 --> 00:40:51,150
You made Endo a national treasure.
你把远藤捧成了国民英雄

815
00:40:51,160 --> 00:40:52,190
